It holds no file of the KCC20 reference and no file copied from its repository. Of the
source text of the reference's contracts it quotes only what 1 lists: names, short
fragments by which the checks name a place, and in the records of the runs the statements
at which the token program stopped. What in it comes from the work of others:

1. What follows the KCC20 reference without being copied from it.

   The contract contracts/TokenVesting.sil reads and writes coins of the KCC20 program of
   the reference, https://github.com/argent-lang/kcc20-reference, revision c8a0871. For
   that it uses, by their names and values: the layout of the state of a KCC20 coin (the
   struct KCC20State: the template field the compiler adds, then amount, owner,
   owner_scheme, borrow_scheme, borrow_guard and extension_commitment, with their types and
   in that order); the prefix and suffix lengths of the KCC20 template, 1 and 3885 bytes,
   which the reference's generated KCC20.sil names gen__const_kcc20_prefix_len and
   gen__const_kcc20_suffix_len; and the owner and borrow schemes it uses (0x00 a Schnorr
   key, 0x04 a covenant id, 0x00 borrowing disabled), which are those of the KCC
   specifications, https://github.com/kaspanet/kccs (CC0). The code is written anew.

   The checks read the reference from a clone the reader makes: its compiled artifact
   through kcc20-family (see 2), and in tests/review_layout.rs its generated KCC20.sil.
   None of its files is included. Where a check expects the token program to refuse, it
   names the place by a few words of the reference's generated source, as the source map
   of kcc20-family prints them, or by that map's rule number K-50. There are five such
   fragments: three parts of conditions, the longest "OpCovInputCount(gen__glob_owner) > 0",
   the start of the statement "validateOutputState(", and the statement "require(false);",
   which several lines of KCC20.sil consist of. The records of the runs in results/*.jsonl
   name every stop in the token program as that source map describes it: the line and the
   statement of the generated KCC20.sil, nine statements of one to four lines in all, for
   example "line 175: require(output_total == input_total); | rule K-37". The comments name
   files and lines of the reference.

   The reference is the work of the contributors of that repository, named in its commit
   history. It is written in Argent (https://github.com/argent-lang/argent) and compiled
   through SilverScript (https://github.com/kaspanet/silverscript), and states its license
   in its Cargo.toml (`license = "ISC"`, revision c8a0871).

2. What comes from kaspa-kcc20-reference-study,
   https://github.com/0xlegacydag/kaspa-kcc20-reference-study, the earlier repository of
   the same copyright holder (ISC License).

   Its crates node-gate (what a Kaspa node says about a transaction without running a
   node: the node's own script engine and mass calculator as dependencies, and the rules
   around them ported from rusty-kaspa; that repository's NOTICE names the ported files)
   and kcc20-family (the reference as data, and the assembler of its calls and coins) are
   dependencies at revision 4d111ff, fetched by cargo and not included here.
   tools/mutation-run.mjs takes the idea of that repository's engine/tools/mutation-run.mjs
   (take one rule away, run the checks again) and is written anew for the source of a
   SilverScript contract. .github/workflows/checks.yml follows the form of that
   repository's workflow and pins the same action at the same commit.

3. rusty-kaspa, https://github.com/kaspanet/rusty-kaspa.

   Nothing in this repository is ported from it: where the code relies on one of its rules,
   it calls the package (check_vesting_genesis in src/launch.rs follows the grouping rule of
   genesis outputs and calls its covenant_id). Its packages are dependencies, fetched by
   cargo and not included here: 12 packages at revision
   a41a333b08848f41bf737b72592e463a6011b8ac in Cargo.lock, and 11 packages of release 2.1.0
   from crates.io in engine-2.1.0/Cargo.lock (ISC License, Copyright (c) 2022-2024 Kaspa
   developers). Comments name its files and lines where the code relies on one of its
   rules.

4. Other Rust dependencies, fetched by cargo and not included here: 2 packages of
   SilverScript, https://github.com/kaspanet/silverscript, at revision 3ed9733 (ISC
   License, Copyright 2026 Kaspa Developers); 4 packages of Argent,
   https://github.com/argent-lang/argent, at revision 9a9f4b1 (ISC License, Copyright 2026
   Argent-lang developers), which kcc20-family uses; and packages from crates.io under
   their own licenses. Every version is pinned by Cargo.lock and engine-2.1.0/Cargo.lock.

Everything else was written for this study and is under the license in the file LICENSE:
